From de3c6021514f355610b31cfa244cbf4de899316e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Drive Player <drive-player@localhost>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 00:49:24 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] mpeg4video: leave stuffing out of the pictures

An encoder at a constant rate pads its stream with stuffing (the start code
0x1C3, then bytes of 0xFF) after a picture that takes less than the rate
allows. The packetizer appended it to the picture being gathered, the one
after it, so that every picture of such a stream began with the stuffing
before it. Stuffing holds nothing a decoder reads, and MediaCodec's MPEG-4
decoder on a MediaTek device (c2.mtk.mpeg4.decoder on a moto g64 5G) took
the first picture that began with it and made no picture again: an MPEG-4
Visual program stream at a recorder's constant rate showed its first few
pictures, then stood still, at the start, after a seek, and for a still.

Drop stuffing as it is found. Its timestamps are not taken from the packet,
so the picture after it in the packet keeps them.
---
 modules/packetizer/mpeg4video.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/modules/packetizer/mpeg4video.c b/modules/packetizer/mpeg4video.c
index 460b585..dd5bff7 100644
--- a/modules/packetizer/mpeg4video.c
+++ b/modules/packetizer/mpeg4video.c
@@ -122,6 +122,7 @@ static unsigned vlc_log2( unsigned int );
 #define STILL_TEXTURE_OBJECT_START_CODE         0x1be
 #define TEXTURE_SPATIAL_LAYER_START_CODE        0x1bf
 #define TEXTURE_SNR_LAYER_START_CODE            0x1c0
+#define STUFFING_START_CODE                     0x1c3
 
 static const uint8_t p_mp4v_startcode[3] = { 0x00, 0x00, 0x01 };
 
@@ -315,6 +316,16 @@ static block_t *ParseMPEGBlock( decoder_t *p_dec, block_t *p_frag )
 #endif
         return NULL;
     }
+    else if( i_startcode == STUFFING_START_CODE )
+    {
+        /* Stuffing pads a stream to its rate, as an encoder at a constant
+         * rate writes it after a picture, and holds nothing a decoder reads.
+         * Left in the picture it came before, it began the block a decoder
+         * was handed, and MediaCodec's MPEG-4 decoder on a MediaTek device
+         * (c2.mtk.mpeg4.decoder) stopped making pictures at the first one. */
+        block_Release( p_frag );
+        return NULL;
+    }
     else
     {
         if( !p_dec->fmt_out.i_extra )
-- 
